module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.list_index_typed_optional_but_realized_as_the_bare_element

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data list_index_typed_optional_but_realized_as_the_bare_element: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "list_index_typed_optional_but_realized_as_the_bare_element" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: one expression has two answers to whether it can be absent. v1.compiler.infer_access check_index_access_node types `xs[i]` (and a keyed `m[k]`) through with_optional_cardinality, because an out-of-range index has no value; the Rust realization of a list index is the bare element, which panics out of range. The type says the consumer must eliminate an absence, and the realized value has no absence to eliminate.",
    "HARM, in both directions. Where the emitter acts on the declared type it emits a coercion the realization cannot satisfy: the note on v1.tokenize code_point_at records `chars[i]` passed to a declared parameter emitting `.expect(..)` on an i64 (E0599), transcribed from that note and not re-executed by the change filing this row. Where a consumer ignores the type, an out-of-range index reaches a Required position: on interpretation as an absent value with no refusal, on the Rust path as a panic. Either way the floor obligation that values inhabit declared types (DESIGN 4b) is not decided for an index value, and any wall that reads cardinality must either refuse code the realization cannot repair or carve the index out.",
    "RECEIPT, gunbc#12791 (2026-09-30), executed. The optional-at-required wall reached the declared-return position and the second-generation regeneration (`claim_executor --required-regen`, the rebuilt seed compiling its own sources) refused with two DeclaredTypeNotInhabited rows, declared Int and produced optional Int, at v1.tokenize source_code_point and v1.tokenize code_point_at, both returning `chars[pos]`. The note on code_point_at had predicted exactly this: the accessors work because return position was not checked, and return-position typechecking would red them together. The wall therefore carries a declared carve-out for index values, whose counted population lives on gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.optional_admitted_where_a_required_value_is_declared.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: `.first()`, `.last()` and `.get(index:)` are typed optional AND eliminated by match in code the same change repaired and compiled, so the disagreement is specific to the index expression form, not to optional collection access in general. The seed's tokenizer depends on the bare realization on its hottest path, which is why the reconciliation is a seed change with a cost question attached and not a consumer rewrite.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT AND CURRENT RUNG: silent, below the floor -- no check decides whether an index value may be absent at the position it reaches, on either path. CEILING: structurally guaranteed; both reconciliations are decidable from modeled facts.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, the capability, either arm sufficient: (a) an index is realized optional on every target wherever it is typed optional, so a match on it is satisfiable and the accessors above eliminate it like any other optional; or (b) an index is admitted only where it is proven in bounds and is then typed as the element, with the unproven form refused. Sufficient for deleting v1.compiler.infer expr_value_is_index_access and the three tokenizer accessors' reliance on an unchecked return. Not satisfied by changing the typing alone or the emission alone, which moves the disagreement rather than removing it.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
